Cloudflare supports DNSSEC, which requires DS record coordination with the registrar when
enabled.
5. DNSSEC Safety Rule
Do not turn DNSSEC on and off repeatedly.
If Cloudflare DNSSEC is enabled:
1. Copy DS record values from Cloudflare.
2. Paste them into GoDaddy / registrar.
3. Wait for propagation.
4. Verify domain resolution.
If DS records are missing or wrong, some users may not reach the domain correctly.
6. SSL Recovery Checklist
If you see ERR_SSL_PROTOCOL_ERROR:
Check:
●
●
●
●
●
●
●
●
Domain added to correct hosting project
A record correct
CNAME correct
SSL certificate issued
DNSSEC DS record correct
Cloudflare SSL mode not misconfigured
Browser cache cleared
Device time correct
Do not assume the AI agent fixed it automatically. Verify in DNS and hosting dashboards.
